OUTPUT
SU2_SCHUR_BRANCH_CONE local_levels=5,6,7,stable_8 k4_formula_checks=65 result=PASS_UNBOUNDED_LOCAL_IDENTITIES

INTERPRETATION
For K>=5, C_2(T_K) is entrywise nonnegative and the checked
coefficient tables prove

  C_2(T_K)^5(e_{1,2}-2e_{0,1})>=0.

The table is stable from K=8 onward because its five-step support
cannot reach label eight.  Nonnegative propagation therefore proves
all powers N>=5 at every level, while the replay checks the only three
smaller powers used in the proof.  At K=4 it verifies the exact
odd-time recurrence residual and the shifted Fibonacci--Lucas
identity.  The document derives the recurrence and closed formula
symbolically and proves their signs for every index.

